Renders feature state that is set in the same frame as a removal from the same
source layer (https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1706).
SourceFeatureState::coalesceChanges() built the frame's changes for each
source layer from the set states, then replaced that entry with the removed
states, so the tiles only heard about the removal. Removing the state of
feature A and setting the state of feature B before one frame cleared A but
left B unchanged on screen until a later frame resent every current state. On
an idle map no such frame comes. The removed states now merge into the set
states, as in GL JS.
Upstream: not proposed

